{"base_rate":0.4464993394980185,"brier":0.14122272126816382,"bss":0.42856661253195116,"bss_hi":0.508297713884237,"bss_lo":0.3408411293504322,"chart":{"base":[448.0,127.6],"fp":[273.1,226.3],"lead":"62,266.9 272,242.3 482,189.5 692,108.8","note":{"base":"skill 0.43 — higher than 81% of cities","fp":"low end +4pp, high end +15pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 76% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 7%; promised 97% → rained 82%"},"rel":"83.2,436.1 376.2,271.5 671.1,111"},"country":"DE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.08892998678996042,"ess":389.9325300170593,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Dortmund</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Dortmund rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>85%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>4%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nWALTROP-ABDINGHOF, 10.1 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.43, ranked 42 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(18&ndash;82) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>218</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>15%</b></td><td class='num'>85</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'><b>38%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>65%</td><td class='num'><b>52%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>72%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>85%</b></td><td class='num'>227</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Dortmund</b> <span class=\"muted\">Germany</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;45% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 45% of days.</p><p>The forecast did clearly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.43</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>18&ndash;82\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Dortmund &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Dortmund\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.9743119266055,378.6605504587156 97.93952941176471,313.4823529411765 179.36459459459462,214.75675675675674 287.54831168831174,107.81818181818181 369.9392105263158,37.15789473684214 410.4093392070485,18.0 410.4093392070485,22.810572687224692 369.9392105263158,89.84210526315786 287.54831168831174,183.45454545454547 179.36459459459462,293.4594594594595 97.93952941176471,364.8705882352941 58.9743119266055,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"219.47424042272127\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"219.47424042272127\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.9743119266055,368.64220183486236 97.93952941176471,326.32941176470587 179.36459459459462,244.27027027027026 287.54831168831174,192.90909090909093 369.9392105263158,118.57894736842104 410.4093392070485,70.91629955947138\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 218 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.9743119266055\" cy=\"368.64220183486236\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 11%&amp;#10;It rained 15% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 85 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"97.93952941176471\" cy=\"326.32941176470587\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 34%&amp;#10;It rained 38% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"179.36459459459462\" cy=\"244.27027027027026\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 65%&amp;#10;It rained 52% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"287.54831168831174\" cy=\"192.90909090909093\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 88%&amp;#10;It rained 72% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"369.9392105263158\" cy=\"118.57894736842104\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 85% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 227 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.4093392070485\" cy=\"70.91629955947138\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(45%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Dortmund the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.51) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.32).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'>0.324</td><td class='num'>12.4%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>53%</td><td class='num'>0.366</td><td class='num'>10.5%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.478</td><td class='num'>9.4%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'>0.509</td><td class='num'>6.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":51.51494,"lon":7.466,"n":757,"n_cities":216,"name":"Dortmund","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.002752293577981652,"n":218,"obs":0.03669724770642202,"sig":true},{"hi":0.20800000000000068,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.1128235294117647,"n":85,"obs":0.15294117647058825,"sig":false},{"hi":0.49,"lo":0.20800000000000068,"mean":0.3428378378378379,"n":74,"obs":0.3783783783783784,"sig":false},{"hi":0.8060000000000008,"lo":0.49,"mean":0.6484415584415585,"n":77,"obs":0.5194805194805194,"sig":true},{"hi":0.9420000000000004,"lo":0.8060000000000008,"mean":0.8811842105263158,"n":76,"obs":0.7236842105263158,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.9420000000000004,"mean":0.9955066079295155,"n":227,"obs":0.8546255506607929,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":10.1,"provisional":false,"rank":42,"rank_hi":82.0,"rank_lo":18.0,"reliability":0.010769748727846154,"resolution":0.11669595813262267,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"dortmund","station":"WALTROP-ABDINGHOF","timezone":"Europe/Berlin"}